Z||000000||Smokin87||01-26-2001||08:50 AM||||i have to change my oil sending unit because of the "bouncy" oil gauge.  3 questions:  1. where is the sending unit on the car, and how do i get to it?  2.  Where can i get a sending unit?  3.  How much will this cost?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_20.jpg"> <BR>Justin Coe||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||01-26-2001||09:02 AM||||Call the dealer and someplace like AutoZone for pricing.  Surprisingly, sometimes the dealer price isn't too bad and you always get OEM reliability.<P>The oil pressure sensor is located between the water pump and the battery.  It is a cylindrical can oriented vertically.  It has a wire connector on top and a steel tube out the bottom.  The tube snakes its way behind the A/C compressor and connects at the base of the oil filter.<P>It usually helps to remove the EGR solenoid assembly to gain access.  Its not a difficult job.<P>You might check the wiring connector on the unit before you go to the trouble of changing it out.  I seem to remember a thread about the vent hole on the top of the unit plugging or something.  Do a search in the archives.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||01-26-2001||09:43 AM||||Here's a link to the Fiero Online Service Guide <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/oil-pressure-sender.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/oil-pressure-sender.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
